{:edb/db-before-t 850 :edb/db-after-t 851 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534163 50 #inst "2026-10-06T06:33:20.708Z" 13194139534163 true] [17592186087639 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279737 13194139534163 true] [17592186087639 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279761 13194139534163 true] [17592186087640 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279744 13194139534163 true] [17592186087640 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279751 13194139534163 true] [17592186087640 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279758 13194139534163 true] [17592186279737 1017 #edb/ref 17592186279738 13194139534163 true] [17592186279737 1089 "q-127826" 13194139534163 true] [17592186279737 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534163 true] [17592186279737 1100 "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534163 true] [17592186279737 1113 #uuid "dd3729c7-43c0-5883-808f-5b63c7f7af84" 13194139534163 true] [17592186279737 1145 "- The matrix $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=-3\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 15=-30.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=7\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 4=2.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ does not have an inverse." 13194139534163 true] [17592186279738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279739 13194139534163 true] [17592186279738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279740 13194139534163 true] [17592186279738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279741 13194139534163 true] [17592186279738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279742 13194139534163 true] [17592186279738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279743 13194139534163 true] [17592186279738 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534163 true] [17592186279738 1041 "selection" 13194139534163 true] [17592186279738 1104 #edb/ref 17592186279740 13194139534163 true] [17592186279738 1110 #uuid "432ab73b-dc